--
Regression test for the for..of + map[k] = map[k] || {} chain. Previously
hit a member_exprt invariant when split() with a non-empty separator on a
non-constant string returned a side_effect_expr_nondett of type double,
which is not a struct/union. Fix: split-with-separator now returns a
nondet array struct of the right shape so the for-of body's
member_exprt{arr, "length", ...} succeeds.
